      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When Susquehanna Township was founded in 1815, Progress stood alone as the only settlement in the township’s southern end.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progress%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Trolley cars once ran along what is now U.S. Route 22 until 1936, when the road was widened for growing automobile traffic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progress%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Progress sits at the intersection of Walnut and Shell Streets and stretches east into the western part of Lower Paxton Township.",
